WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.004 --> 00:00:16.915
Aladdin changed after his experience in the treasury.

2
00:00:18.196 --> 00:00:20.178
He didn't feel like a child anymore.

3
00:00:21.339 --> 00:00:23.380
He didn't want to play all day in the streets.

4
00:00:25.102 --> 00:00:27.604
He felt grown up and wanted to help his mother.

5
00:00:30.556 --> 00:00:33.038
Aladdin looked at the plates that had held their food.

6
00:00:33.759 --> 00:00:35.380
And he had an idea.

7
00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:39.243
"I will take one of these plates to the bazaar and sell it."

8
00:00:40.465 --> 00:00:44.908
"It's a fine plate, but it's probably not real gold," said Zeba.

9
00:00:44.928 --> 00:00:48.251
"You might get a few copper coins for it."

10
00:00:50.133 --> 00:00:53.295
Aladdin put the plate in his jacket and went to the bazaar.

11
00:00:54.516 --> 00:00:58.520
He found an old merchant in a shop filled with pots, plates, and cups.

12
00:01:00.876 --> 00:01:02.457
"How much will you give me for this plate?"

13
00:01:03.658 --> 00:01:04.958
Aladdin asked the merchant.

14
00:01:06.779 --> 00:01:09.721
The old man took the plate and looked at it closely.

15
00:01:09.741 --> 00:01:14.544
"Pure gold," he whispered to himself.

16
00:01:16.065 --> 00:01:20.547
He looked up at Aladdin and thought, "But I think this boy does not know this."

17
00:01:23.109 --> 00:01:27.171
To Aladdin, he said slyly, "It is not a bad plate.

18
00:01:27.591 --> 00:01:29.052
How much do you want for it?"

19
00:01:30.092 --> 00:01:30.772
"What is it worth?"

20
00:01:31.413 --> 00:01:32.133
asked Aladdin.

21
00:01:33.774 --> 00:01:37.535
The old man smiled and pulled one gold piece from his pocket.

22
00:01:37.555 --> 00:01:40.456
"Oh, thank you, sir!"

23
00:01:41.157 --> 00:01:43.137
Aladdin cried, taking the coin.

24
00:01:44.578 --> 00:01:47.359
Immediately the merchant wished he had offered even less.

25
00:01:47.379 --> 00:01:52.141
"Two copper coins would have been enough," he thought.

26
00:01:54.542 --> 00:01:58.664
After that, whenever Aladdin needed money, he took a plate to the merchant.

27
00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:04.802
Each time, the old man grumbled to himself and paid one gold coin.

28
00:02:07.103 --> 00:02:11.445
One day, Aladdin put the last plate in his jacket and headed for the bazaar.

29
00:02:12.745 --> 00:02:16.487
As he walked along, another merchant came out of a different shop.

30
00:02:16.507 --> 00:02:22.249
"Boy, I have seen you passing by many times," he said.

31
00:02:22.269 --> 00:02:26.651
"And you always go to that one old merchant.

32
00:02:27.971 --> 00:02:29.272
Show me what you are selling.

33
00:02:29.684 --> 00:02:30.804
Maybe I will pay more."

34
00:02:30.824 --> 00:02:36.746
"Oh, I get a very good price for my plates," said Aladdin with pride.

35
00:02:38.206 --> 00:02:40.847
The new merchant took Aladdin's plate and weighed it.

36
00:02:42.107 --> 00:02:44.788
"Is this plate like the ones you sold to the old man?"

37
00:02:44.808 --> 00:02:47.869
"Yes," replied Aladdin.

38
00:02:47.889 --> 00:02:49.009
"Exactly the same."

39
00:02:49.029 --> 00:02:51.250
"What did he give you?"

40
00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:52.950
asked the new merchant.

41
00:02:52.970 --> 00:02:55.651
"One gold coin!"

42
00:02:56.411 --> 00:02:58.252
said Aladdin with a big smile.

43
00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:01.982
"He cheated you," the merchant said.

44
00:03:02.002 --> 00:03:04.464
"This plate is pure gold.

45
00:03:04.904 --> 00:03:07.006
It is worth one hundred gold coins!"

46
00:03:07.026 --> 00:03:12.790
"I am a fool," muttered Aladdin, his face red.

47
00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:16.132
"And that old man has been laughing at me!"

48
00:03:16.152 --> 00:03:20.996
"Ah, but you can learn from your mistake," said the merchant.

49
00:03:23.137 --> 00:03:26.420
From that day, Aladdin went to the bazaar every morning.

50
00:03:27.788 --> 00:03:29.930
He talked to all the merchants and traders.

51
00:03:31.030 --> 00:03:33.172
He learned about buying and selling.

52
00:03:34.453 --> 00:03:37.535
He asked many questions and learned the value of things.

53
00:03:39.597 --> 00:03:43.399
Aladdin sometimes visited a merchant who sold diamonds and rubies.

54
00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:49.104
He listened to everything the man said and watched him buy and sell.

55
00:03:50.465 --> 00:03:54.668
That is how Aladdin learned his glass fruit were not glass at all.

56
00:03:56.140 --> 00:04:00.943
They were rare stones worth more than anything owned by the sultan himself.

57
00:04:03.024 --> 00:04:06.206
One morning, Aladdin went to the bazaar as usual.

58
00:04:07.647 --> 00:04:13.230
When he arrived, he saw one of the sultan's men on a large horse speaking to the crowd.

59
00:04:13.250 --> 00:04:15.691
"People of the city!"

60
00:04:16.151 --> 00:04:17.032
the man shouted.

61
00:04:18.333 --> 00:04:20.314
"Lock up your shops and go home!

62
00:04:21.334 --> 00:04:23.756
Whoever does not obey will be killed!"
